                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nFirst, we need to understand that medical abortion involves the use of drugs to terminate a pregnancy. The most commonly used drugs for medical abortion are mifepristone and misoprostol.\n\nNext, we need to consider the timing of the pregnancy. The patient is 6 weeks pregnant, which means that the pregnancy is still in the early stages. Medical abortion is most effective when used in the first 9 weeks of pregnancy.\n\nBased on this information, the correct answer is D) Mifepristone. This drug is used in combination with misoprostol to induce a medical abortion. It works by blocking the hormone progesterone, which is necessary for the pregnancy to continue. Misoprostol is then used to cause contractions and expel the pregnancy.\n\nMegestrol (A) is a progestin hormone used to treat certain types of cancer and appetite loss. Tamoxifen (B) is a selective estrogen receptor modulator used to treat breast cancer. Terbutaline (C) is a beta-agonist used to treat asthma and premature labor. None of these drugs are used for medical abortion.\n\nThe copper intrauterine device (E) is a form of long-acting reversible contraception that can be inserted into the uterus to prevent pregnancy. It is not used for medical abortion.",
                        "answers": [
