                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nStep 1: Identify the reason for the patient's visit\nThe patient is concerned about a recent pregnancy and wants to medically abort it.\n\nStep 2: Determine the appropriate drug for medical abortion\nThe drug commonly used for medical abortion is Mifepristone, also known as RU-486. It is a progesterone receptor antagonist that blocks the action of progesterone, which is necessary for the maintenance of pregnancy. Mifepristone is usually given in combination with Misoprostol, a prostaglandin analog that causes uterine contractions and expulsion of the pregnancy.\n\nStep 3: Eliminate the incorrect options\nA) Megestrol is a progestin used to treat breast cancer and endometrial cancer. It is not used for medical abortion.\nB) Tamoxifen is a selective estrogen receptor modulator used to treat breast cancer. It is not used for medical abortion.\nC) Terbutaline is a beta-2 adrenergic agonist used to treat asthma and premature labor. It is not used for medical abortion.\nE) Copper intrauterine device (IUD) is a long-acting reversible contraceptive that can be used for emergency contraception up to 5 days after unprotected intercourse. It is not used for medical abortion.\n\nStep 4: Choose the correct answer\nThe correct answer is D) Mifepristone.",
