                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: Medical abortion is a safe and effective method of terminating a pregnancy using medication. It involves taking two drugs, mifepristone and misoprostol, which work together to end the pregnancy. Mifepristone is taken first, followed by misoprostol 24-48 hours later. The procedure is typically done up to 10 weeks of pregnancy.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What is medical abortion?\n2. What drugs are used in medical abortion?\n3. When is medical abortion typically done?\n4. Which drug should be administered to this patient for medical abortion?\n\nAnswers:\n1. Medical abortion is a safe and effective method of terminating a pregnancy using medication.\n2. The drugs used in medical abortion are mifepristone and misoprostol.\n3. Medical abortion is typically done up to 10 weeks of pregnancy.\n4. The drug that should be administered to this patient for medical abortion is D) Mifepristone.",
                        "answers": [
