                    {
                        "id": "847609ce-cedd-4ad6-b7e4-385a3e7f524b",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": "qa-16",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: The lymphatic system plays a crucial role in the spread of cancer cells throughout the body. Ovarian cancer commonly metastasizes to the lymph nodes in the pelvis and abdomen before spreading to distant sites such as the lungs and brain.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What is the sentinel node?\n2. What are the lumbar trunks and cisterna chyli?\n3. What are the bronchomediastinal trunk and lymphatic duct?\n4. What is the thoracic duct?\n5. What is the subclavian vein?\n6. Which lymphatic route would ovarian cancer most likely take to metastasize to the brain?\n\nAnswers:\n1. The sentinel node is the first lymph node to which cancer cells are most likely to spread from a primary tumor.\n2. The lumbar trunks are lymphatic vessels that drain lymph from the lower limbs, pelvis, and abdominal wall. The cisterna chyli is a sac-like structure at the base of the thoracic duct where lymph from the lumbar trunks and intestinal trunk converge.\n3. The bronchomediastinal trunk is a lymphatic vessel that drains lymph from the thorax and upper abdomen. The lymphatic duct is a vessel that drains lymph from the right side of the head, neck, and upper limb, as well as the right side of the thorax and abdomen.\n4. The thoracic duct is the largest lymphatic vessel in the body, which drains lymph from the lower limbs, pelvis, abdomen, left side of the thorax, and left side of the head and neck.\n5. The subclavian vein is a large vein that receives blood from the arms and head and returns it to the heart.\n6. Based on the location of the ovarian cancer and the lymphatic drainage patterns, the most likely lymphatic route for this malignancy to have metastasized to the brain is option D: Sentinel node - right lumbar trunk - cisterna chyli - thoracic duct - right subclavian vein - systemic circulation.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "e99c155b-dbb9-4ef7-be36-76981158f832",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-E",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "D) Sentinel node - right lumbar trunk - cisterna chyli - thoracic duct - right subclavian vein - systemic circulation.",
                                "correct_answer": false
                            }
                        ],
