                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: The presentation of fever, dyspnea, grayish-white pseudomembrane in the oropharynx, and cervical lymph node enlargement suggests a possible diagnosis of diphtheria.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What is diphtheria?\nDiphtheria is a bacterial infection caused by Corynebacterium diphtheriae.\n\n2. How is diphtheria transmitted?\nDiphtheria is spread through respiratory droplets or contact with contaminated objects.\n\n3. What are the symptoms of diphtheria?\nSymptoms of diphtheria include fever, sore throat, difficulty breathing, and the formation of a grayish-white pseudomembrane in the throat.\n\n4. How is diphtheria treated?\nDiphtheria is treated with antibiotics and antitoxin.\n\nAnswer: B) Gram-positive bacteria producing exotoxin that acts via ADP ribosylation. The presentation of fever, dyspnea, grayish-white pseudomembrane in the oropharynx, and cervical lymph node enlargement suggests a possible diagnosis of diphtheria, which is caused by Corynebacterium diphtheriae. This bacteria produces an exotoxin that acts via ADP ribosylation, leading to the formation of the pseudomembrane and other symptoms.",
