udent: So, which statement is correct?\n\nProfessor: The correct statement is E) This patient has no contraindications for bupropion and may safely use it. Since the patient does not have a history of seizure disorder and is not currently taking any antiepileptic medication, bupropion is a safe option for him to try for smoking cessation. However, it's important to monitor him for any potential side effects and to make sure he is not experiencing any worsening of his GERD",
