 Choose the most likely diagnosis.\nBased on the patient's symptoms and physical examination findings, the most likely diagnosis is lichen sclerosus. However, lichen planus and atrophic vaginitis are also possible diagnoses and should be considered in the differential. Further testing, such as a biopsy, may be necessary to confirm the diagnosis.",
