                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "The correct answer is D) Hydrochlorthiazide.\n\nHydrochlorthiazide is a thiazide diuretic that is used to treat hypertension and edema. It works by inhibiting the reabsorption of sodium and chloride in the distal renal tubule, which leads to increased excretion of water and sodium. This results in decreased blood volume and decreased blood pressure.",
