                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Plan:\n1. Define glomerular capillaries and their function in the kidney.\n2. Analyze each statement and determine if it is true or false based on the function of glomerular capillaries.\n3. Identify the statement that is not true and explain why.\n\nAnswer:\n1. Glomerular capillaries are tiny blood vessels located in the kidneys that filter waste products and excess fluid from the blood to form urine.\n2. \nA) The oncotic pressure of the fluid leaving the capillaries is less than that of fluid entering it - False. The oncotic pressure of the fluid leaving the capillaries is greater than that of fluid entering it due to the selective filtration of small molecules.\nB) Glucose concentration in the capillaries is the same as that in glomerular filtrate - True. Glucose is a small molecule that is filtered through the glomerular capillaries and is reabsorbed in the proximal tubule.\nC) Constriction of afferent arteriole decreases the blood flow to the glomerulus - True. Constriction of the afferent arteriole reduces the blood flow to the glomerulus, which decreases the glomerular filtration rate.\nD) Hematocrit of the fluid leaving the capillaries is less than that of the fluid entering it - False. The hematocrit of the fluid leaving the capillaries is the same as that of the fluid entering it because red blood cells are too large to be filtered through the glomerular capillaries.\n\nTherefore, the statement that is not true about glomerular capillaries is D) Hematocrit of the fluid leaving the capillaries is less than that of the fluid entering it.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "7c4aed76-30be-4f22-b455-c1301e1333db",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
