                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "The correct answer is A) The oncotic pressure of the fluid leaving the capillaries is less than that of fluid entering it.\n\nTo determine which statement is not true about glomerular capillaries, we need to evaluate each statement individually.\n\nA) The oncotic pressure of the fluid leaving the capillaries is less than that of fluid entering it. This statement is not true. The oncotic pressure of the fluid leaving the capillaries is greater than that of fluid entering it. This is because the glomerular capillaries are highly permeable to water and small solutes, but not to larger molecules like proteins. As a result, proteins remain in the capillaries, increasing the oncotic pressure of the blood and causing water to be reabsorbed into the capillaries.\n\nB) Glucose concentration in the capillaries is the same as that in glomerular filtrate. This statement is true. Glucose is a small molecule that is freely filtered by the glomerular capillaries. As a result, the concentration of glucose in the glomerular filtrate is the same as that in the capillaries.\n\nC) Constriction of afferent arteriole decreases the blood flow to the glomerulus. This statement is true. The afferent arteriole is the main site of resistance in the renal circulation. Constriction of the afferent arteriole decreases the blood flow to the glomerulus, which in turn decreases the glomerular filtration rate.\n\nD) Hematocrit of the fluid leaving the capillaries is less than that of the fluid entering it. This statement is true. The glomerular capillaries are highly permeable to water and small solutes, but not to larger molecules like red blood cells. As a result, the hematocrit of the fluid leaving the capillaries is lower than that of the fluid entering it.\n\nTherefore, the statement that is not true about glomerular capillaries is A) The oncotic pressure of the fluid leaving the capillaries is less than that of fluid entering it.",
