                        "cot": "\n\nC) Histopathological examination for Negri bodies\n\nThe presence of Negri bodies, which are eosinophilic, intracytoplasmic inclusions in the neurons of the brain, is a hallmark of rabies infection. Therefore, histopathological examination of the corneal impression for the presence of Negri bodies is the most accurate test for diagnosing rabies. Indirect immunofluorescence and antibodies against Rabies virus can also be used for diagnosis, but they may not be as accurate as histopathological examination. PCR for virus can be used to detect the presence of viral RNA, but it may not be as sensitive as histopathological examination for detecting the virus.",
