                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Plan:\n1. Understand what measles is and how it progresses.\n2. Identify the different stages of measles.\n3. Determine the duration of each stage.\n4. Compare the options given and choose the one that matches the correct isolation period of measles.\n\nAnswer: D) Eruptive stage until 7th day of rash.\n\nExplanation: Measles is a highly contagious viral infection that spreads through the air when an infected person coughs or sneezes. The infection progresses through different stages, including the incubation period, prodromal phase, and eruptive stage.\n\nDuring the prodromal phase, which lasts for 2-4 days, the infected person experiences symptoms such as fever, cough, runny nose, and red eyes. The eruptive stage follows, during which a rash appears on the face and spreads to the rest of the body. The rash lasts for about 5-6 days and then fades away.\n\nTo prevent the spread of measles, infected individuals should be isolated for a certain period. According to the options given, the correct isolation period is D) Eruptive stage until 7th day of rash. This means that the infected person should be isolated from the onset of the rash until the rash has been present for 7 days.",
