                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Rephrased question: What is the duration of the isolation period for measles?\n\nStep-by-step reasoning:\n\n- Measles is a highly contagious viral infection.\n- To prevent the spread of the disease, infected individuals should be isolated for a certain period of time.\n- The isolation period is usually based on the duration of the infectious stage of the disease.\n- The infectious stage of measles is generally considered to be from a few days before the onset of symptoms (prodromal stage) to a few days after the appearance of the rash (eruptive stage).\n- Therefore, the isolation period for measles should cover this entire period of infectiousness.\n\nAnswer: D) Eruptive stage until 7th day of rash.",
