                        "cot_trigger": "zhou-01",
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nStep 1: Understand the concept of resuscitation\nResuscitation refers to the process of reviving a person who has stopped breathing or whose heart has stopped beating. It involves a series of interventions aimed at restoring normal breathing and circulation.\n\nStep 2: Identify the key parameters for monitoring during resuscitation\nDuring resuscitation, several parameters need to be monitored to assess the effectiveness of the interventions. These include:\n\n- Airway patency and adequacy of ventilation\n- Circulation, including heart rate, blood pressure, and urine output\n- Oxygenation, as measured by the saturation of oxygen in the blood\n- Fluid balance, including the volume and composition of fluids administered\n\nStep 3: Evaluate the options provided in the question\nThe question asks for the best guide for the management of resuscitation. The options provided are:\n\nA) CVP (central venous pressure)\nB) Urine output\nC) Blood pressure\nD) Saturation of Oxygen\n\nOf these options, only one directly measures the effectiveness of the interventions aimed at restoring normal breathing and circulation, which is the saturation of oxygen in the blood (option D). While the other parameters (CVP, urine output, and blood pressure) are important to monitor during resuscitation, they do not provide as direct an indication of the success of the interventions.\n\nStep 4: Select the correct answer\nBased on the above analysis, the correct answer is D) Saturation of Oxygen.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "85dadb8a-aa35-4f09-b753-b7ff868164e2",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
