                        "cot_trigger": "kojima-01",
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": " The first thing you need to do in a resuscitation is to assess the patient. This includes taking their vital signs and looking for any obvious signs of distress. Once you have a baseline, you can start to think about what might be causing the problem.\n\nIf the patient is not breathing, the first step is to start CPR. If the patient is breathing but their oxygen levels are low, you may need to give them supplemental oxygen. If the patient's blood pressure is low, you may need to give them fluids or medications to raise it. And finally, if the patient's heart rate is abnormal, you may need to give them medications to stabilize it.",
