                        "cot": "\n\nThe correct answer is D) AntiHAV IgMantiHBC, AntiHCV, AntiHEV.\n\nThe patient's symptoms and LFT results suggest acute viral hepatitis. To confirm the diagnosis and determine the specific virus causing the infection, the following tests should be ordered:\n\n- AntiHAV IgM: This test detects the presence of IgM antibodies against the hepatitis A virus, which indicates acute infection with the virus.\n- IgM antiHBC: This test detects the presence of IgM antibodies against the hepatitis B core antigen, which indicates acute or recent infection with the hepatitis B virus.\n- AntiHCV: This test detects the presence of antibodies against the hepatitis C virus, which indicates past or current infection with the virus.\n- AntiHEV: This test detects the presence of antibodies against the hepatitis E virus, which is a common cause of acute viral hepatitis in developing countries.\n\nBy performing these tests, the specific virus causing the patient's symptoms can be identified, which will help guide treatment and management.",
