                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": " \n\nThe three embryonic germ layers are ectoderm, mesoderm, and endoderm. \n\nEctoderm gives rise to the outermost layer of the skin, the nervous system, and the sense organs. \n\nMesoderm gives rise to the muscles, bones, blood, and reproductive organs. \n\nEndoderm gives rise to the lining of the digestive tract, the respiratory tract, and the urinary tract. \n\nNow, let's think about where these three layers come from. \n\nThe ectoderm is derived from the epiblast. The mesoderm is derived from the hypoblast. The endoderm is derived from the hypoblast.",
