                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "it is important to understand the embryonic development of the blastocyst. The blastocyst is a hollow ball of cells that forms about 5-6 days after fertilization. It consists of an outer layer of cells called the trophoblast, which will eventually form the placenta, and an inner cell mass (ICM), which will give rise to the embryo and its supporting structures.\n\nThe ICM is further divided into two layers: the epiblast and the hypoblast. The epiblast is the upper layer of cells and gives rise to the three embryonic germ layers: ectoderm, mesoderm, and endoderm. The hypoblast is the lower layer of cells and contributes to the formation of the yolk sac.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is C) Ectoderm and mesoderm are derived from the epiblast, while endoderm is derived from the hypoblast.",
                        "answers": [
