                        "cot": "\n\n1. Identify the question: What type of natural disaster causes the maximum deaths?\n\n2. Review the options: \nA) Hydrological \nB) Meteorological \nC) Geological \nD) Fires \n\n3. Determine the correct answer: \n\nTo determine the correct answer, we need to consider the number of deaths caused by each type of natural disaster. \n\nAccording to a report by the Centre for Research on the Epidemiology of Disasters (CRED), between 1995 and 2015, the top three natural disasters that caused the most deaths were: \n\n1. Hydrological disasters (such as floods and landslides) - 157,000 deaths per year on average \n2. Meteorological disasters (such as storms and heatwaves) - 18,000 deaths per year on average \n3. Geological disasters (such as earthquakes and volcanic eruptions) - 8,000 deaths per year on average \n\nFires were not included in the top three natural disasters that caused the most deaths. \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is A) Hydrological. \n\n4. Provide the answer: The natural disaster that causes the maximum deaths is Hydrological (option A).",
