                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Rephrased question: What factors contribute to a baby being considered high risk?\n\nStep-by-step reasoning:\n\n- A) Working mother: This factor alone does not necessarily make a baby high risk. Many working mothers have healthy pregnancies and give birth to healthy babies.\n- B) Antenatal preeclampsia: This is a condition that can cause high blood pressure and damage to organs in the mother, which can affect the baby's growth and development. Therefore, a baby whose mother has antenatal preeclampsia would be considered high risk.\n- C) Third child: This factor alone does not necessarily make a baby high risk. The number of children a mother has does not necessarily impact the health of the baby.\n- D) Twins: Twins are considered high risk because they are more likely to be born prematurely and have a lower birth weight, which can lead to health complications.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is B) Antenatal preeclampsia and D) Twins.",
