                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nThe question is asking about a sampling method that is used for selecting patients based on potential factors that may affect the results. This suggests that the sampling method needs to take into account some sort of stratification or grouping of patients based on these factors.\n\nA) Systematic random sampling: This method involves selecting every nth patient from a list or population. It does not take into account any potential factors that may affect the results, so it is not the correct answer.\n\nB) Simple random sampling: This method involves randomly selecting patients from a list or population. While it is a valid sampling method, it does not take into account any potential factors that may affect the results, so it is not the correct answer.\n\nC) Stratified random sampling: This method involves dividing the population into strata or groups based on potential factors that may affect the results, and then randomly selecting patients from each stratum. This is the correct answer, as it takes into account the potential factors that may affect the results.\n\nD) Cluster sampling: This method involves dividing the population into clusters or groups, and then randomly selecting entire clusters to include in the sample. It is not the best choice for selecting patients based on potential factors that may affect the results, as it may not ensure a representative sample of patients within each cluster.",
