                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "The answer is C) Stratified random sampling.\n\nStratified random sampling is used for selecting patients with respect to potential factors that will affect the results. This method involves dividing the population into subgroups or strata based on certain characteristics, such as age, gender, or disease status. Then, a random sample is selected from each stratum in proportion to its size in the population. This ensures that the sample is representative of the population and that any potential factors that may affect the results are accounted for. \n\nSystematic random sampling involves selecting every nth individual from a list or population, which may not account for potential factors that could affect the results. \n\nSimple random sampling involves selecting individuals randomly from the population without any consideration for potential factors that could affect the results. \n\nCluster sampling involves selecting groups or clusters of individuals from the population, which may not account for potential factors that could affect the results.",
