                    {
                        "id": "a5092bcc-4931-432d-a49b-b7d67969d6c8",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": "qa-17",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: Can you explain what is meant by \"selecting patients with respect to potential factors\"?\n\nProfessor: Sure. When selecting patients for a study, researchers often want to make sure that the patients they choose have certain characteristics or factors that could affect the results of the study. For example, if a study is looking at the effectiveness of a new medication, researchers might want to make sure that the patients they choose have similar ages, genders, and medical histories.\n\nStudent: Okay, I understand. So which sampling method is used for this type of selection?\n\nProfessor: The sampling method that is used for selecting patients with respect to potential factors is called stratified random sampling.\n\nStudent: Can you explain how stratified random sampling works?\n\nProfessor: Sure. With stratified random sampling, the population is divided into subgroups, or strata, based on certain characteristics or factors. Then, a simple random sample is taken from each stratum. This ensures that the sample is representative of the entire population and that the characteristics or factors of interest are evenly represented in the sample.\n\nStudent: That makes sense. So what about the other sampling methods listed in the question?\n\nProfessor: Systematic random sampling involves selecting every nth individual from a list or population. Simple random sampling involves selecting individuals at random from the population. Cluster sampling involves selecting groups, or clusters, of individuals from the population. These methods may be useful in certain situations, but they do not specifically address the need to select patients with respect to potential factors.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "38ac3ca1-4f23-44a6-8b47-ab6140bdd720",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "C) Stratified random sampling.",
                                "correct_answer": true
                            }
                        ],
