                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "A) Complete blood counts: This test is important to check for any infections or anemia that could be causing the altered sensorium. So, this test should be done.\n\nB) Random blood sugar: Altered sensorium can be caused by hypo- or hyperglycemia. Therefore, checking blood sugar levels is important. So, this test should be done.\n\nC) Lumbar puncture: This test is used to check for meningitis or other central nervous system infections that could cause altered sensorium. However, it is not the first test to be done and should only be performed after other potential causes have been ruled out and if there is a strong suspicion of meningitis. So, this test may not be necessary in all cases.\n\nD) Non-contrast CT head: This test is important to rule out any intracranial pathologies like hemorrhage, tumors, or infarctions that could be causing the altered sensorium. So, this test should be done.\n\nBased on this analysis, the answer is C) Lumbar puncture, as it is not a necessary test in all cases and should only be performed after other potential causes have been ruled out.",
