                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Plan:\n1. Assess the patient's vital signs and level of consciousness.\n2. Obtain a detailed medical history and perform a physical examination.\n3. Order appropriate diagnostic tests based on the patient's presentation.\n4. Evaluate the results of the tests to determine the underlying cause of the altered sensorium.\n\nAnswer:\nBased on the plan, the answer to the question is C) Lumbar puncture. While a lumbar puncture may be indicated in certain cases of altered sensorium, it is not a routine test and should only be done if there is suspicion of meningitis or encephalitis. The other tests listed (complete blood counts, random blood sugar, and non-contrast CT head) are commonly ordered to help diagnose the cause of altered sensorium.",
