                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "The patient presents to the emergency with altered sensorium. The question asks which test should NOT be done. Let's go through each option:\n\nA) Complete blood counts: This test can help identify any abnormalities in the blood, such as infections or anemia, that may be causing the altered sensorium. This test should be done.\n\nB) Random blood sugar: This test can help identify if the patient has high or low blood sugar levels, which can cause altered sensorium. This test should be done.\n\nC) Lumbar puncture: This test involves inserting a needle into the spinal canal to collect cerebrospinal fluid (CSF) for analysis. It can help diagnose infections or bleeding in the brain that may be causing the altered sensorium. This test should be done.\n\nD) Non-contrast CT head: This test uses X-rays to create detailed images of the brain and can help identify any bleeding or swelling that may be causing the altered sensorium. However, the question asks which test should NOT be done. Therefore, the answer is D) Non-contrast CT head. This test may not be necessary in all cases and may be avoided if the patient has contraindications to CT scan or if the clinical suspicion is low.",
                        "answers": [
