                        "cot": "\n\nD) Chorionic villous biopsy\n\nChorionic villous biopsy is the most accurate test to assess the risk of Down's syndrome in the present pregnancy. It involves taking a small sample of the placenta and analyzing the chromosomes of the fetal cells. This test can detect Down's syndrome with a high degree of accuracy, but it carries a small risk of miscarriage. Other tests such as maternal alpha-feto protein, maternal HCG, and USG can provide some information about the risk of Down's syndrome, but they are not as accurate as chorionic villous biopsy.",
