                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "What is the type of cry that is not a cry at all, with no tears or sobs, just a constant whining noise?\n\nStep-by-step reasoning:\n\n- The question is asking for a type of cry that does not involve tears or sobs, but rather a constant whining noise.\n- Option A, obstinate cry, does not necessarily fit this description, as obstinacy implies a stubborn refusal to comply rather than a vocalization.\n- Option B, frighten cry, also does not fit, as fear usually involves more than just whining, such as trembling, shaking, or hiding.\n- Option C, hurt cry, is a possibility, as pain or discomfort can sometimes elicit a whining sound without tears or sobs.\n- Option D, compensatory cry, does not seem to be a likely answer, as compensation usually implies making up for something or balancing out a loss, which does not relate to crying.\n\nTherefore, the answer is C) Hurt cry.",
