                        "cot_trigger": "kojima-01",
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": " First, what is the definition of lateral movement? Lateral movement is defined as movement away from the midline of the body. So, in order for the condyle to move laterally, the muscle that contracts must be on the same side of the body as the condyle. This rules out option C. \n\nNext, we need to think about which muscle is responsible for lateral movement of the condyle. The lateral pterygoid muscle is responsible for lateral movement of the condyle. This muscle is located on the side of the face, just behind the cheekbone. The lateral pterygoid muscle has two heads: the medial head and the lateral head. The medial head is located on the same side of the body as the condyle, while the lateral head is located on the opposite side of the body. Therefore, the correct answer is option B.",
                        "answers": [
