                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nStep 1: Understand the question and the given information.\nThe question is asking about the muscle responsible for the lateral movement of the condyle. The options given are Contralateral lateral pterygoid, Ispilateral lateral pterygoid, Same side medial pterygoid, and None of the above.\n\nStep 2: Recall the anatomy and function of the muscles involved.\nThe lateral pterygoid muscle is responsible for the lateral movement of the mandible. It has two heads, the superior head, and the inferior head. The superior head of the lateral pterygoid muscle helps to protrude the mandible, while the inferior head helps to retract the mandible. The medial pterygoid muscle is responsible for elevating the mandible and moving it from side to side.\n\nStep 3: Analyze the options given.\nOption A states that the contralateral lateral pterygoid muscle is responsible for the lateral movement of the condyle. This is incorrect because the contralateral lateral pterygoid muscle is on the opposite side of the mandible and is responsible for protrusion of the mandible.\n\nOption B states that the ipsilateral lateral pterygoid muscle is responsible for the lateral movement of the condyle. This is correct because the ipsilateral lateral pterygoid muscle is on the same side of the mandible and is responsible for lateral movement of the mandible.\n\nOption C states that the same side medial pterygoid muscle is responsible for the lateral movement of the condyle. This is incorrect because the medial pterygoid muscle is responsible for elevating the mandible and moving it from side to side, but not for lateral movement of the condyle.\n\nOption D states that none of the above muscles are responsible for the lateral movement of the condyle. This is incorrect because as discussed in option B, the ipsilateral lateral pterygoid muscle is responsible for the lateral movement of the condyle.\n\nStep 4: Select the correct option.\nBased on the analysis, the correct option is B) Ispilateral lateral pterygoid.",
