                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "To rephrase the question: What is the topic of Ewing's postulates?\n\nStep-by-step reasoning:\n\n- Ewing's postulates are a set of criteria used to determine whether a tumor is malignant or not.\n- Therefore, the topic of Ewing's postulates is related to tumors.\n- Option A is about growth at the site following trauma, which is not necessarily related to tumors.\n- Option B is about growth after a neurological injury, which is also not necessarily related to tumors.\n- Option C is about age-related changes in the teeth, which is not related to tumors at all.\n- Option D is about old seminal stains, which is completely unrelated to the topic of Ewing's postulates.\n- Therefore, the correct answer is none of the above.\n\nThe right answer: None of the above.",
