                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "The answer is A) Glucose-6-phosphatase.\nIn this condition, the child likely has a deficiency of glucose-6-phosphatase, which is needed to release glucose from glycogen. When given after a meal, glucagon causes the release of glucose from glycogen, so the child's blood glucose level rises. When given after an overnight fast, glucagon does not cause a rise in blood glucose level because there is no glycogen to release glucose from.",
