                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": " Pharyngeal pseudosulcus is a condition in which the walls of the pharynx become thickened and narrowed. It is usually caused by an underlying condition.\n\nA) Vocal Abuse: Vocal abuse can cause vocal cord nodules, but it is not known to cause pharyngeal pseudosulcus.\n\nB) Laryngopharyngeal Reflux: Laryngopharyngeal reflux is a condition in which stomach acid backs up into the throat and can cause inflammation of the pharynx. This can lead to pharyngeal pseudosulcus.\n\nC) Tuberculosis: Tuberculosis is an infectious disease caused by the bacteria Mycobacterium tuberculosis. It can cause inflammation of the pharynx, which can lead to pharyngeal pseudosulcus.\n\nD) Corticosteroid usage: Corticosteroids are medications used to reduce inflammation. They can be used to treat conditions that cause inflammation of the pharynx, which can lead to pharyngeal pseudosulcus.\n\nAnswer: B, C, and D",
