                        "cot": " An autopsy was performed, which means the person is already dead. Two linear fractures were found on the petrous part of the temporal bone. This means that the person suffered a blow to the head, which caused the fractures.\n\nNow, we need to determine which rule gives the sequence of fractures. McNaughton's rule states that the order of fractures is from the point of impact to the point of exit. Puppe's rule states that the order of fractures is from the point of impact to the base of the skull. Young's rule states that the order of fractures is from the base of the skull to the point of impact. Dunlop's rule states that the order of fractures is from the point of exit to the point of impact.\n\nIn this case, the order of fractures is from the point of impact to the point of exit, so the correct answer is A) McNaughton's rule.",
