                        "cot": "\n\nA) High speed film: This option is incorrect because high speed film actually increases patient radiation. This is because it requires less exposure time, but the radiation dose per exposure is higher.\n\nB) Intensifying screens: This option is correct. Intensifying screens are used to reduce patient radiation by reducing the amount of radiation needed to produce an image. They work by converting X-rays into visible light, which then exposes the film.\n\nC) Lead apron: This option is also correct. Lead aprons are used to shield the patient's body from unnecessary radiation exposure during the radiographic procedure.\n\nD) Decreasing kVp: This option is incorrect. Decreasing kVp (kilovoltage peak) will actually increase patient radiation because it will require more exposure time to produce an image.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is D) Decreasing kVp.",
