                        "cot": "the contaminated debris should be removed from the avulsed tooth. The correct treatment option in this case would be A) Clean root surface with saline and reimplant. The root surface should be gently cleaned with saline solution to remove any debris or contaminants. The tooth should then be reimplanted as soon as possible to increase the chances of successful reattachment. Follow-up treatment may include a root canal procedure or other restorative measures depending on the extent of damage to the tooth.",
