                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Step 1: Assess the situation\nAn 8-year-old child has experienced trauma, resulting in the avulsion of their central incisor. The tooth has been contaminated with debris and 20 minutes have passed since the incident.\n\nStep 2: Determine the appropriate treatment\nIn cases of avulsed permanent teeth, the best prognosis for successful reimplantation is when the tooth is replanted as soon as possible, ideally within 5-10 minutes. However, since 20 minutes have passed, it is still worth attempting reimplantation.\n\nStep 3: Clean the tooth\nThe tooth has been contaminated with debris, so it is essential to clean the root surface before reimplantation. The best method for cleaning the tooth in this situation is to gently rinse the root surface with saline solution (option A).\n\nStep 4: Reimplant the tooth\nAfter cleaning the root surface with saline, the tooth should be reimplanted into the socket. It is important not to scrub or curette the root surface, as this can damage the periodontal ligament cells, which are crucial for successful reimplantation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is A) Clean root surface with saline and reimplant.",
                        "answers": [
