                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "The correct answer is A) Clean root surface with saline and reimplant.\n\nStep 1: Assess the situation - An 8-year-old child has had trauma and has lost their central incisor tooth. The tooth has been avulsed and has been contaminated with debris.\n\nStep 2: Evaluate the options - The options are A) Clean root surface with saline and reimplant, B) Clean and curette root surface and reimplant, C) Clean root surface, do RCT and reimplant, and D) Scrubbing of root surface and reimplant.\n\nStep 3: Eliminate the incorrect options - Option B involves curetting the root surface, which can cause damage to the root and is not recommended. Option C involves doing a root canal treatment, which is not necessary in this case as the tooth is not infected. Option D involves scrubbing the root surface, which can also cause damage to the root and is not recommended.\n\nStep 4: Choose the correct option - Option A involves cleaning the root surface with saline, which is a gentle and effective way to remove debris and contaminants. Reimplanting the tooth is also important to ensure that it has the best chance of survival.\n\nStep 5: Justify the answer - Cleaning the root surface with saline is a safe and effective way to remove debris and contaminants without causing damage to the root. Reimplanting the tooth is important to ensure that it has the best chance of survival. Doing a root canal treatment or curetting the root surface is not necessary in this case and can cause further damage to the tooth. Therefore, option A is the correct answer.",
