                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: Professor, can you explain what avulsed means?\n\nProfessor: Sure, avulsed means that the tooth has been completely knocked out of the socket.\n\nStudent: Okay, so what does contaminated with debris mean?\n\nProfessor: It means that there is dirt or other foreign material on the tooth that needs to be removed before it can be reimplanted.\n\nStudent: Got it. So what is the best treatment option for the child?\n\nProfessor: The best treatment option would be to clean the root surface with saline and reimplant the tooth. This will help to remove any debris and reduce the risk of infection.\n\nStudent: Why not just scrub the root surface?\n\nProfessor: Scrubbing the root surface can actually damage the root and make it more difficult for the tooth to reattach. That's why it's better to clean it with saline, which is a gentler option.\n\nStudent: And why not do a root canal treatment?\n\nProfessor: A root canal treatment is not necessary in this case because the tooth is still alive and can be reimplanted successfully. If the tooth had been dead for a while, then a root canal treatment would be necessary.\n\nStudent: Okay, I understand. Thank you, Professor!",
                        "answers": [
