                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nStep 1: Assess the situation and gather information\n- An 8 year old child has had trauma and lost their central incisor\n- The tooth has been avulsed for 20 minutes and is contaminated with debris\n- The child has rushed to a dental clinic with the avulsed tooth\n\nStep 2: Consider the options\n- A) Clean root surface with saline and reimplant\n- B) Clean and curette root surface and reimplant\n- C) Clean root surface, do RCT and reimplant\n- D) Scrubbing of root surface and reimplant\n\nStep 3: Eliminate options that are not appropriate\n- Option D (scrubbing of root surface) is not recommended as it can damage the root surface and reduce the chances of successful reimplantation.\n\nStep 4: Evaluate remaining options\n- Option A (clean root surface with saline and reimplant) is a good option for a tooth that has been avulsed for less than 60 minutes and is not contaminated with debris. However, in this case, the tooth is contaminated with debris, so this option may not be sufficient.\n\n- Option B (clean and curette root surface and reimplant) involves removing any debris or tissue from the root surface and then reimplanting the tooth. This may be a good option for this case as it addresses the contamination issue.\n\n- Option C (clean root surface, do RCT and reimplant) involves performing a root canal treatment before reimplantation. This may be necessary if the tooth has been avulsed for a longer period of time or if there is significant damage to the tooth. However, in this case, it may not be necessary.\n\nStep 5: Choose the best option\n- Based on the information provided, option B (clean and curette root surface and reimplant) seems to be the best option for this case. It addresses the contamination issue and is less invasive than option C (clean root surface, do RCT and reimplant). \n\nStep 6: Follow up\n- After reimplantation, the child should be monitored closely for any signs of infection or other complications. They should also be advised on proper oral hygiene and follow-up appointments with the dentist.",
