                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nThe patient's HbsAg is non-reactive, which means they do not have an active hepatitis B virus infection. \n\nThe HBV DNA is undetectable, which further confirms that there is no active infection. \n\nThe HbeAg is also non-reactive, which indicates that the patient is not highly infectious. \n\nHowever, the IgG anti-HbC is reactive, which means that the patient has been exposed to the hepatitis B virus in the past and has developed antibodies against it. \n\nBased on these findings, the likely cause of the abnormal findings is chronic hepatitis recovery state. The patient has previously been infected with hepatitis B virus, but has cleared the infection and is now in a recovery state.",
