                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "First, let's identify the vector or mode of transmission for each disease:\n\nA) Kala Azar - Also known as visceral leishmaniasis, this disease is transmitted by the bite of infected female sandflies.\n\nB) Chandipura encephalitis - This viral disease is transmitted by the bite of infected sandflies.\n\nC) Babesiosis - This disease is caused by a parasite that infects red blood cells and is transmitted by the bite of infected ticks, specifically Ixodes scapularis and Ixodes pacificus.\n\nD) Carrion's Disease - Also known as bartonellosis, this disease is caused by the bacteria Bartonella bacilliformis and is transmitted by the bite of infected sandflies.\n\nNow, let's identify which disease is NOT transmitted by sandflies:\n\nThe correct answer is C) Babesiosis, as it is transmitted by ticks, not sandflies.",
