                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Based on the given information, the most likely cause of the patient's symptoms is concussion.\n\nHere's the reasoning:\n\n- The patient has a history of fall and vomiting near an alcohol shop, which suggests that he may have been under the influence of alcohol at the time of the incident. However, this alone does not explain his current symptoms.\n- The fact that the patient is awake with open eyes indicates that he is not in a coma or vegetative state. This rules out diffuse axonal injury, which is a severe form of traumatic brain injury that often results in coma or vegetative state.\n- The presence of retrograde amnesia (i.e., inability to remember events that occurred before the injury) is a common symptom of concussion. This suggests that the patient has suffered a mild traumatic brain injury.\n- Cerebral venous thrombosis is a rare condition that can cause headache, seizures, and focal neurological deficits. However, it is not a likely cause of the patient's symptoms based on the given information.\n\nTherefore, the most likely cause of the patient's symptoms is concussion.",
