                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "What is the most likely cause of a 40-year-old male with a history of fall and one episode of vomiting near an alcohol shop, who was brought to casualty and was awake with open eyes and had retrograde amnesia?\n\nStep-by-step reasoning:\n\n- The patient had a fall and vomited near an alcohol shop, suggesting that he may have been under the influence of alcohol.\n- He was brought to casualty, which means he was likely in need of medical attention.\n- He was awake with open eyes, which indicates that he was conscious and alert.\n- He had retrograde amnesia, which means he could not remember events that occurred before the injury.\n- Based on these symptoms, the most likely cause could be either drunkenness or a head injury.\n\nAnswer: C) Drunkenness",
