                    {
                        "id": "296e86a5-0d04-4c0a-a57a-dc8f098d013e",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": "qa-12",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "The Krebs cycle is a metabolic pathway that involves the oxidation of acetyl-CoA to produce energy in the form of ATP. Acetyl-CoA is formed from the breakdown of carbohydrates, fats, and proteins. In the case of proteins, amino acids are converted to acetyl-CoA or other intermediates that can enter the Krebs cycle.\n\nTo determine which amino acid does not enter the Krebs cycle by forming Acetyl-CoA pyruvate, we need to examine the metabolic pathways of each amino acid.\n\nA) Glycine: Glycine can be converted to serine, which can then be converted to pyruvate. Pyruvate can then be converted to acetyl-CoA, which can enter the Krebs cycle. Therefore, glycine can enter the Krebs cycle by forming Acetyl-CoA pyruvate.\n\nB) Tyrosine: Tyrosine can be converted to fumarate, which can enter the Krebs cycle. Therefore, tyrosine can enter the Krebs cycle by forming Acetyl-CoA pyruvate.\n\nC) Hydroxyproline: Hydroxyproline is a modified form of proline, which can be converted to pyruvate. Pyruvate can then be converted to acetyl-CoA, which can enter the Krebs cycle. Therefore, hydroxyproline can enter the Krebs cycle by forming Acetyl-CoA pyruvate.\n\nD) Alanine: Alanine can be converted to pyruvate, which can then be converted to acetyl-CoA. However, this conversion does not involve the formation of Acetyl-CoA pyruvate. Therefore, alanine does not enter the Krebs cycle by forming Acetyl-CoA pyruvate.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is D) Alanine.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "81f73d39-a2ba-4bf6-8615-ccf2060bc254",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
