                "id": "b4d9ead1-e3c7-446d-b49b-7e4dcbdada18",
                "ref_id": "",
                "question": "Golgi tendon organs detect:",
                "type": "multiplechoice",
                "choices": [
                    "Static muscle length",
                    "Dynamic muscle length",
                    "Muscle tension",
                    "Muscle action"
                ],
                "context": "",
                "cot": [
                    "STRUCTURE OF GOLGI TENDON ORGAN\nGolgi tendon organ\u00a0 is\u00a0 situated\u00a0 in\u00a0 the\u00a0 tendon\u00a0 of skeletal\u00a0 muscle near the attachment of extrafusal fibers. It is placed in series between the muscle fibers and the\u00a0 tendon. Golgi tendon organ is formed by a group of nerve endings covered by a connective tissue capsule.\nNERVE SUPPLY TO GOLGI TENDON ORGAN\nSensory nerve fiber supplying the Golgi tendon organ belongs to Ib type. The nerve fiber supplying Golgi tendon organ ramifies into many branches. Each branch ends in the form of a knob.\u00a0\nFUNCTIONS OF GOLGI TENDON ORGAN\nGolgi tendon organ gives response to the change in the force or tension developed in the skeletal muscle during contraction. It is also the receptor for inverse stretch reflex and lengthening reaction and thereby prevents damage of muscle due to overstretching."
                ],
                "answer": [
                    "Muscle tension"
                ],
