                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nStep 1: Understand what Golgi tendon organs are\nGolgi tendon organs are sensory receptors located in the tendons of muscles. They are responsible for detecting changes in muscle tension.\n\nStep 2: Eliminate incorrect options\nOption A, static muscle length, is not detected by Golgi tendon organs. This is because they are located in the tendons and not in the muscle fibers themselves.\nOption B, dynamic muscle length, is also not detected by Golgi tendon organs. This is because they are not sensitive to changes in muscle length, only changes in muscle tension.\nOption D, muscle action, is too broad and does not specifically relate to what Golgi tendon organs detect.\n\nStep 3: Choose the correct option\nOption C, muscle tension, is the correct answer. Golgi tendon organs are sensitive to changes in muscle tension, which is the force exerted by the muscle against the tendon. When muscle tension increases, the Golgi tendon organs send signals to the spinal cord, which in turn causes the muscle to relax and reduce tension. This is a protective mechanism to prevent muscle damage from excessive tension.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "4edae1d4-49cd-4a3a-af73-cf0005fdfd3a",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
