                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Golgi tendon organs (GTOs) are sensory receptors located in tendons, which are the connective tissues that attach muscles to bones. Their primary function is to detect changes in muscle tension.\n\nA) Static muscle length - This is not the primary function of GTOs, as they are more concerned with muscle tension rather than muscle length.\n\nB) Dynamic muscle length - Although GTOs may indirectly detect changes in muscle length due to changes in tension, their primary function is not to detect dynamic muscle length.\n\nC) Muscle tension - This is the primary function of GTOs. They detect changes in muscle tension and help regulate muscle force to prevent injury.\n\nD) Muscle action - GTOs do not directly detect muscle action, but rather the tension generated by muscle action.\n\nSo, the correct answer is:\n\nC) Muscle tension",
                        "answers": [
                            {
