                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "The Golgi tendon organs are sensory receptors located in the tendons of muscles. They are responsible for detecting changes in muscle tension. Therefore, the correct answer is C) Muscle tension. \n\nTo break it down further, when a muscle contracts, it generates tension that is transmitted through the tendon to the Golgi tendon organ. The Golgi tendon organ then sends signals to the spinal cord and brain, which can adjust the muscle tension accordingly. This feedback loop helps to prevent excessive muscle contraction and potential injury. \n\nIn contrast, static muscle length refers to the length of a muscle when it is at rest, while dynamic muscle length refers to the changes in muscle length during movement. Muscle action is a broad term that can refer to any type of muscle activity, including contraction, relaxation, and stretching. Therefore, options A, B, and D are incorrect.",
