                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: Professor, can you explain what Golgi tendon organs are?\n\nProfessor: Sure, Golgi tendon organs are sensory receptors located in the tendons of muscles.\n\nStudent: What do they detect?\n\nProfessor: They detect muscle tension.\n\nStudent: So, does that mean the answer is C?\n\nProfessor: Yes, that's correct. The answer is C) Muscle tension. \n\nStudent: Can you explain how they detect muscle tension?\n\nProfessor: When a muscle contracts, it pulls on the tendon, which activates the Golgi tendon organ. The organ then sends a signal to the spinal cord, which in turn sends a signal back to the muscle to relax. This is a protective mechanism to prevent the muscle from tearing due to excessive tension.\n\nStudent: That makes sense. Thank you for explaining it step by step.",
