                        "cot": "\n\n1. Read the question carefully: The question is asking what Golgi tendon organs detect.\n\n2. Understand the options: The options are static muscle length, dynamic muscle length, muscle tension, and muscle action.\n\n3. Recall knowledge: Golgi tendon organs are sensory receptors located in tendons that detect changes in muscle tension.\n\n4. Eliminate options: Static and dynamic muscle length are not detected by Golgi tendon organs. Muscle action is too broad and does not specifically relate to the function of Golgi tendon organs.\n\n5. Choose the correct answer: The correct answer is C) Muscle tension.\n\nFinal answer: Golgi tendon organs detect muscle tension.",
