                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "To calculate the net filtration pressure, we can use the Starling equation:\n\nNet filtration pressure = (capillary hydrostatic pressure - interstitial hydrostatic pressure) - (capillary oncotic pressure - interstitial oncotic pressure)\n\nWe are given the following values:\n\nInterstitial hydrostatic pressure = 2 mm Hg\nInterstitial oncotic pressure = 7 mm Hg\nCapillary hydrostatic pressure = 25 mm Hg\nNet filtration pressure = 3 mm Hg\n\nWe need to find the capillary oncotic pressure (COP). Let's plug in the values and solve for COP:\n\n3 = (25 - 2) - (COP - 7)\n3 = 23 - (COP - 7)\n3 = 23 - COP + 7\nCOP = 23 + 7 - 3\nCOP = 27 mm Hg\n\nSo the correct answer is D) 27.",
                        "answers": [
