                        "cot": "\n\nNet filtration pressure = (capillary hydrostatic pressure + interstitial oncotic pressure) - (capillary oncotic pressure + interstitial hydrostatic pressure)\n\nWe know that net filtration pressure should be 3 mm Hg, interstitial hydrostatic pressure is 2 mm Hg, interstitial oncotic pressure is 7 mm Hg, and capillary hydrostatic pressure is 25 mm Hg. Let's plug in these values and solve for capillary oncotic pressure:\n\n3 = (25 + 7) - (capillary oncotic pressure + 2)\n\n3 = 32 - capillary oncotic pressure - 2\n\n3 = 30 - capillary oncotic pressure\n\ncapillary oncotic pressure = 27 mm Hg\n\nTherefore, the answer is D) 27.",
