                        "cot": "Rephrased question: What is the capillary oncotic pressure needed to achieve a net filtration pressure of 3 mm Hg, given the interstitial hydrostatic pressure of 2 mm Hg, interstitial oncotic pressure of 7 mm Hg, and capillary hydrostatic pressure of 25 mm Hg?\n\nStep-by-step reasoning:\n- Net filtration pressure = (capillary hydrostatic pressure + interstitial oncotic pressure) - (capillary oncotic pressure + interstitial hydrostatic pressure)\n- Substituting the given values: 3 mm Hg = (25 mm Hg + 7 mm Hg) - (capillary oncotic pressure + 2 mm Hg)\n- Simplifying: 3 mm Hg = 30 mm Hg - (capillary oncotic pressure + 2 mm Hg)\n- Rearranging: capillary oncotic pressure = 30 mm Hg - 3 mm Hg - 2 mm Hg\n- Solving: capillary oncotic pressure = 25 mm Hg\n\nTherefore, the answer is D) 27.",
