                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: Professor, can you please tell me what is the period of pre operational stage according to Piaget's theory?\n\nProfessor: Sure, the period of pre operational stage according to Piaget's theory is from 2-6 years of age.\n\nStudent: How did Piaget come up with this theory?\n\nProfessor: Piaget observed children and their cognitive development and came up with a theory that explains how children's thinking changes as they grow.\n\nStudent: What are some characteristics of the pre operational stage?\n\nProfessor: In the pre operational stage, children have egocentric thinking, they struggle with conservation, and they have difficulty with abstract thinking.\n\nStudent: Can you explain what conservation means?\n\nProfessor: Conservation is the understanding that even if the appearance of an object changes, the object still remains the same. For example, if you pour water from a tall glass into a short glass, the amount of water is still the same.\n\nStudent: I see, so how does this relate to the pre operational stage?\n\nProfessor: Children in the pre operational stage struggle with conservation because they focus on the appearance of objects rather than the actual amount. They may think that the water in the short glass is less because it looks like it is less.\n\nStudent: Thank you for explaining that, professor. I understand it better now.",
                        "answers": [
