                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "X-Linked Severe Combined Immunodeficiency (SCID) is a rare genetic disorder that affects the immune system. It is caused by mutations in the IL2RG gene, which provides instructions for making a protein that is essential for the development and function of immune cells.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What is X-Linked SCID?\n2. What causes X-Linked SCID?\n3. What is the IL2RG gene?\n4. What is the function of the protein made by the IL2RG gene?\n5. Which of the given genes is involved in X-Linked SCID?\n\nAnswers:\n1. X-Linked SCID is a rare genetic disorder that affects the immune system.\n2. X-Linked SCID is caused by mutations in the IL2RG gene.\n3. The IL2RG gene provides instructions for making a protein that is essential for the development and function of immune cells.\n4. The protein made by the IL2RG gene is a component of several receptors on the surface of immune cells that are involved in signaling pathways critical for immune cell development and function.\n5. The gene involved in X-Linked SCID from the given options is D) IL2RG.",
                        "answers": [
