                        "cot_trigger": "zhou-01",
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "A) Catalase: This enzyme is involved in breaking down hydrogen peroxide, which is produced by immune cells to kill microbes. However, catalase itself is not directly involved in killing microbes.\n\nB) Oxidase: This enzyme is involved in producing reactive oxygen species (ROS), which are used by immune cells to kill microbes. This seems like a possible answer.\n\nC) Lysozyme: This enzyme is involved in breaking down the cell walls of bacteria, leading to their destruction. However, it is not directly involved in intracellular killing of microbes.\n\nD) IL6: This is a cytokine involved in the immune response, but it is not directly involved in killing microbes.\n\nBased on this information, the best answer is B) Oxidase, as it is involved in producing ROS, which are used by immune cells to kill microbes intracellularly.",
                        "answers": [
