                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "it is important to note that the patient's injury occurred while playing hockey, which is a high-impact sport that can cause significant trauma to the knee joint. Based on the presentation of instability in full extension but not at 90 degrees of flexion, the most likely structure that is damaged is the anterior cruciate ligament (ACL).\n\nOf the options given, the most likely location of the ACL tear is the anteromedial portion (B). The posterolateral portion (A) is less commonly injured, and the posterior cruciate ligament (C) typically presents with instability at 90 degrees of flexion rather than full extension. The anterior horn of the medial meniscus (D) may also be injured in a knee injury, but it would not present with the same pattern of instability as an ACL tear.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is B) Anteromedial portion of the anterior cruciate ligament.",
