                        "cot": "\n\nThe formula for pulmonary compliance is:\n\nCompliance = change in volume / change in pressure\n\nThe change in volume is the tidal volume, which is 500 mL. The change in pressure is the difference between the intrapleural pressure before and after inspiration, which is:\n\n-9 cmH2O - (-4 cmH2O) = -5 cmH2O\n\nHowever, we need to convert this pressure difference to units of liters, since the tidal volume is in liters. 1 cmH2O is equivalent to 0.098 kPa, and 1 liter is equivalent to 1000 mL, so:\n\n-5 cmH2O x 0.098 kPa/cmH2O x 1 L/1000 mL = -0.0049 L\n\nNow we can calculate the compliance:\n\nCompliance = 500 mL / (-0.0049 L) = -102.04 mL/cmH2O\n\nHowever, the answer choices are in units of L/cm, so we need to convert:\n\n-102.04 mL/cmH2O x 1 L/1000 mL = -0.102 L/cmH2O\n\nSince compliance is a positive value, we can take the absolute value:\n\nCompliance = 0.102 L/cmH2O\n\nTherefore, the answer is C) 0.2 L/cm.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "6bb3992a-c902-433b-af51-7cb619f7159b",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "C) 0.2 L/cm.",
                                "correct_answer": false
                            }
                        ],
