                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Pulmonary compliance is calculated as the change in lung volume (\u0394V) divided by the change in intrapleural pressure (\u0394P). In this case, the tidal volume is 500 mL, which is equal to 0.5 L. The change in intrapleural pressure is -9 cm of water - (-4 cm of water) = -5 cm of water.\n\nCompliance = \u0394V / \u0394P = 0.5 L / 5 cm of water = 0.1 L/cm\n\nSo, the correct answer is A) 0.1 L/cm.",
