                        "cot": "\n\nStep 1: Calculate the change in intrapleural pressure during inspiration.\n\n\u0394P = P after inspiration - P before inspiration\n\u0394P = (-9 cmH2O) - (-4 cmH2O)\n\u0394P = -5 cmH2O\n\nStep 2: Calculate the pulmonary compliance using the formula:\n\nCompliance = Tidal volume / \u0394P\n\nCompliance = 500 mL / (-5 cmH2O)\nCompliance = -100 mL/cmH2O\n\nStep 3: Convert the compliance to liters per centimeter.\n\nCompliance = -100 mL/cmH2O x 1 L/1000 mL\nCompliance = -0.1 L/cmH2O\n\nStep 4: Round the answer to the nearest tenth.\n\nThe pulmonary compliance in this patient is 0.1 L/cm. Therefore, the correct answer is A) 0.1 L/cm.",
