                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: What is the name of the test where the examiner places one hand under the patient's heel and the patient is asked to raise his other leg against downward resistance?\n\nProfessor: That test is called the heel raise test.\n\nStudent: What is the purpose of the heel raise test?\n\nProfessor: The purpose of the heel raise test is to assess the strength of the patient's lower limbs.\n\nStudent: What is the name of the specific test where the examiner places one hand under the patient's heel and the patient is asked to raise his other leg against downward resistance?\n\nProfessor: That specific test is called the Hoover test.\n\nStudent: Can you explain how the Hoover test is performed?\n\nProfessor: Sure. The examiner places one hand under the patient's heel and the patient is asked to raise his other leg against downward resistance. If the patient is able to raise the leg against resistance, it indicates that the patient is using both legs to perform the movement. If the patient is unable to raise the leg against resistance, it indicates that the patient is not using both legs to perform the movement and may have weakness in one of the legs.\n\nStudent: Okay, I understand. And what are the other options for the name of this test?\n\nProfessor: The other options are Waddell's test, O'Donoghue test, and McBride test. However, those tests are used for different purposes and involve different movements. The correct answer for this specific test is the Hoover test.",
