                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "C) Check for response and call help.\n\nThe first thing to do when presented with an unresponsive patient is to check for a response. This can be done by gently tapping the patient's shoulder and asking if they are okay. If there is no response, the next step is to call for help. This can be done by activating the emergency response system or calling for assistance from nearby medical professionals. Once help is on the way, further assessment and treatment can be provided as necessary. It is important to prioritize calling for help before beginning any other interventions, as time is critical in emergency situations. Therefore, option C is the correct answer. Options A, B, and D may be necessary in certain situations, but they should not be the first step taken.",
                        "answers": [
