                        "cot": "\n\nThe neonatal mortality rate is calculated by dividing the number of neonatal deaths by the total number of live births (excluding stillbirths) and multiplying by 1,000.\n\nNeonatal mortality rate = (Number of neonatal deaths / Total number of live births) x 1,000\n\nTotal number of live births = 12,450 - 212 = 12,238\n\nNeonatal mortality rate = (450 / 12,238) x 1,000 = 36.76\n\nRounding to the nearest whole number, the neonatal mortality rate for this population in 2012 is 37.\n\nTherefore, the closest option is A) 36.",
