                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "A) Enterobius vermicularis: This is a pinworm, and autoinfection can occur when eggs are transferred from the anus to the mouth, either directly or indirectly through contaminated surfaces or objects. So, autoinfection can be caused by this helminth.\n\nB) Hymenolepis nana: This is a tapeworm, and autoinfection can occur when eggs are ingested, either directly from contaminated hands or indirectly through contaminated food or water. So, autoinfection can be caused by this helminth.\n\nC) Taenia solium: This is also a tapeworm, but autoinfection is not common with this helminth. Infection usually occurs by ingesting undercooked pork containing cysticerci (larval stage), which then develop into adult tapeworms in the intestine. Autoinfection is not a typical feature of Taenia solium infection.\n\nD) Ascaris lumbricoides: This is a roundworm, and autoinfection can occur when eggs are ingested, either directly from contaminated hands or indirectly through contaminated food or water. So, autoinfection can be caused by this helminth.\n\nBased on this information, the correct answer is:\n\nC) Taenia solium",
