                    {
                        "id": "048416b8-4110-4038-8e87-149458824837",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": null,
                        "cot_trigger": "zhou-01",
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "A) DNA repair: DNA repair mechanisms, such as base excision repair and nucleotide excision repair, occur in the 5' to 3' direction.\n\nB) DNA replication: DNA replication occurs in the 5' to 3' direction, with the leading strand being synthesized continuously and the lagging strand being synthesized in fragments (Okazaki fragments).\n\nC) RNA editing: RNA editing can occur in both 5' to 3' and 3' to 5' directions, depending on the specific editing event and enzyme involved.\n\nD) Transcription: Transcription occurs in the 5' to 3' direction, with RNA polymerase synthesizing the RNA transcript based on the DNA template strand.\n\nBased on this information, the correct answer is:\n\nC) RNA editing",
                        "answers": [
