                        "cot_trigger": "kojima-03",
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "it is important to understand what a positive pivot shift test is. It is a clinical test used to diagnose instability in the knee joint, specifically in cases of anterior cruciate ligament (ACL) injury. During the test, the examiner applies a valgus force to the knee while it is flexed, and then rotates the tibia externally. If the tibia subluxates anteriorly, and then reduces with a palpable clunk, it is considered a positive pivot shift test.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is B) Anterior cruciate ligament.",
                        "answers": [
