                        "cot_trigger": "zhou-01",
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "A positive pivot shift test is used to assess the stability of the knee joint, specifically focusing on the anterior cruciate ligament (ACL). The test is performed by flexing and extending the knee while applying a valgus force and internal rotation to the lower leg. A positive result indicates instability and possible injury to the ACL.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is:\nB) Anterior cruciate ligament",
                        "answers": [
