                        "cot": "\n\nEpistaxis is a medical condition in which bleeding occurs from the nose. To control epistaxis, various vessels in the nasal cavity are ligated. The vessels that are commonly ligated include the sphenopalatine artery, anterior ethmoidal artery, and maxillary artery. However, the internal carotid artery is not ligated in case of epistaxis control as it is a major artery that supplies blood to the brain and ligation of this artery can lead to serious complications. Therefore, the correct answer is option C) Internal carotid artery.",
