                        "cot": "\n\nStep 1: Identify the research question\nThe research question is to compare the fat content in the expressed breast milk of pre-term infants and term infants.\n\nStep 2: Consider the study designs\nA) Case control: This study design compares individuals with a particular condition (cases) to those without the condition (controls). This design is not suitable for this research question as it does not involve comparing the fat content in the expressed breast milk of pre-term and term infants.\n\nB) Prospective cohort: This study design follows a group of individuals over time to observe the development of a particular condition or outcome. This design is not suitable for this research question as it does not involve following individuals over time.\n\nC) Longitudinal study: This study design involves following a group of individuals over time to observe changes in a particular outcome. This design is suitable for this research question as it involves comparing the fat content in the expressed breast milk of pre-term and term infants over time.\n\nD) Ambispective: This study design involves collecting data from both retrospective and prospective sources. This design is not suitable for this research question as it does not involve collecting data from both retrospective and prospective sources.\n\nStep 3: Choose the best study design\nThe best study design for this research question is a longitudinal study. Therefore, the answer is C) Longitudinal study.",
