                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Step 1: Read the question and the answer choices carefully.\nStep 2: Identify the correct acronym for APGAR.\nStep 3: Compare the answer choices to determine which one matches the correct acronym.\nStep 4: Explain the reasoning behind the correct answer.\n\nStep 1: The question is asking for the acronym that stands for APGAR.\nStep 2: The correct acronym for APGAR is Activity, Pulse, Grimace, Appearance, and Respiration.\nStep 3: \n\nA) Activity, pulse pressure, grimace, appearance, rate of respiration - This answer choice includes all the correct components of the APGAR acronym, so it could be a possible answer.\nB) Appearance, pressure, grimace, MAP, hea rate - This answer choice includes some of the correct components, but it is missing two important ones (pulse and respiration), so it cannot be the correct answer.\nC) Appearance, pressure, grimace, appearance, rate of hea beat - This answer choice includes some of the correct components, but it repeats \"appearance\" and it uses \"heart beat\" instead of \"respiration,\" so it cannot be the correct answer.\nD) Appearance, pulse, grimace, activity, respiration - This answer choice includes all the correct components of the APGAR acronym, so it could be a possible answer.\n\nStep 4: The correct answer is either A or D, as they both include all the correct components of the APGAR acronym. However, the correct answer is A because it uses \"rate of respiration\" instead of just \"respiration.\" The APGAR score is a quick assessment tool used to evaluate the physical condition of a newborn immediately after birth. The five components of the APGAR score are Activity, Pulse, Grimace, Appearance, and Rate of Respiration. Each component is scored on a scale of 0 to 2, with a maximum score of 10. The APGAR score is used to determine if the newborn needs any immediate medical attention or if they are in good health.",
