                "id": "764c0c80-b716-45a1-9fe7-b13588090401",
                "ref_id": "",
                "question": "Central value of a set of 180 values can be obtained by",
                "type": "multiplechoice",
                "choices": [
                    "2nd tertile",
                    "90th percentile",
                    "2nd quartile",
                    "9th decile"
                ],
                "context": "",
                "cot": [
                    "Quartile: Divides a distribution into 4 equal parts, so the number of intercepts required will be 3, i.e. Q1, Q2, Q3\n\n\u2013 So, Zero \u2013 Q1 covers 25% values\n\u2013 Similarly, Q2 \u2013 Q1, Q3 \u2013 Q2 and 100 \u2013 Q3 all cover 25% values each\n\u2013 Thus, Q2 \u2013 Zero, 100 \u2013 Q2 and Q3 \u2013 Q1 all cover 50% values each\n\u2013 Q1 divides a distribution in a ratio of 25 : 75 OR 1 : 3\n\u2013 Q2 divides a distribution in a ratio of 50 : 50 OR 1 : 1, Thus second quartile is equivalent to median\n\u2013 Q3 divides a distribution in a ratio of 75 : 25 OR 3 : 1.\nIn the given question, n = 180\nThus Q2 which is equivalent to median, divides a distribution in a ratio of 50 : 50 OR 1 : 1."
                ],
                "answer": [
                    "2nd quartile"
                ],
                "generated_cot": [
