                "question": "Considering the latent period of muscle twitch to be 10 ms, contraction time 40 ms and relaxation time 50 ms, what will be the tetanizing frequency for this muscle?",
                "type": "multiplechoice",
                "choices": [
                    "25 Hz",
                    "50 Hz",
                    "100 Hz",
                    "75 Hz"
                ],
                "context": "",
                "cot": [
                    "Ans: A. 25 HzStimulation frequency at which summation of contractions occurs -Determined by twitch duration of the paicular muscle under study.Example:If twitch duration = 10 ms.Frequencies less than 1/10 ms (100/s) - Cause discrete responses interrupted by complete relaxation.Frequencies greater than 100/s cause summation.Tetany:Continuous contraction of muscle fibers, without latent period & relaxation time.Hence tetanizing frequency depends only on contraction time, i.e. twitch duration.Twitch duration = 40 milliseconds = 0.04 secTetanizing frequency = 1/0.04 = 25 Hz"
                ],
                "answer": [
                    "25 Hz"
                ],
                "generated_cot": [
