                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: Hi Professor, I have a question about saving money. I want to start saving money for a vacation at the end of the year. What's the best way to do that?\n\nProfessor: Well, there are a few ways to save money. Can you tell me what you've already considered?\n\nStudent: Yes, I looked over my budget and expenses and I think the best way to save money is to cut back on some things.\n\nProfessor: That's a good start. What are some things you could cut back on?\n\nStudent: I was thinking about quitting eating lunch out.\n\nProfessor: That's a great idea. How much do you usually spend on lunch?\n\nStudent: About $10 a day.\n\nProfessor: Okay, so if you bring your lunch from home instead, you could save $50 a week. That's $200 a month and $2400 a year.\n\nStudent: Wow, that's a lot of money. What else could I do to save money?\n\nProfessor: Another thing you could do is make more phone calls instead of texting or using data. Do you use a lot of data on your phone?\n\nStudent: Yes, I do. How much could I save by making more phone calls?\n\nProfessor: Well, it depends on your phone plan, but if you're using a lot of data, you could save $20 or $30 a month by making more phone calls instead.\n\nStudent: Okay, that makes sense. Is there anything else I could do to save money?\n\nProfessor: You could also try to buy less with monopoly money. That way, you won't be spending as much on things you don't really need.\n\nStudent: I'm not sure I understand. What do you mean by monopoly money?\n\nProfessor: I mean things like gift cards or store credit. If you have a gift card for a store, you might be tempted to spend more than you need to just because you have the gift card. So, if you try to buy less with those types of things, you'll save money in the long run.\n\nStudent: Oh, I see. That's a good idea. Is there anything else I could do?\n\nProfessor: One more thing you could do is have lunch with friends instead of going out to eat. That way, you can split the cost of the meal and save money.\n\nStudent: That's a good idea too. Thanks for all the tips, Professor. I think I have a good plan for saving money now.",
