                        "cot_trigger": "kojima-01",
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nFirst, it's important to understand the basics of genetics and how eye color is inherited. Eye color is determined by multiple genes, but the most important one is called OCA2. This gene comes in two versions: a brown version (B) and a blue version (b). Brown is dominant over blue, so if a person inherits at least one brown version of the gene, they will have brown eyes. However, if they inherit two blue versions of the gene, they will have blue eyes.\n\nWith this in mind, the best way to guess a baby's eye color is to look at the eye colors of their parents. If both parents have brown eyes, there is a high chance that the baby will also have brown eyes. However, if one or both parents have blue eyes, there is a chance that the baby could inherit two blue versions of the OCA2 gene and have blue eyes as well.\n\nIt's important to note that eye color can be unpredictable, especially if there is a history of different eye colors in the family. While it's possible to make an educated guess based on the parents' eye colors, there is no guarantee that the baby will have the same eye color.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "71742724-8598-4f65-af1d-ca377b7e3826",
