                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: Can you explain option A more? How do surroundings affect eye color?\n\nProfessor: Sure. The surroundings a baby is born in can affect their eye color because the amount of light they are exposed to can impact the production of melanin in their eyes. More exposure to light can lead to more melanin production, resulting in darker eye color.\n\nStudent: And what about option B? How does a parent's diet affect their baby's eye color?\n\nProfessor: There is no scientific evidence to support the idea that a parent's diet can directly affect their baby's eye color. Eye color is determined by genetics, specifically the genes that control the production of melanin in the iris.\n\nStudent: So, if eye color is determined by genetics, does that mean option D is the best way to guess a baby's eye color?\n\nProfessor: Yes, that's correct. Looking at the genealogy records of a baby's family can give you a good idea of what their eye color might be. Eye color is an inherited trait, so if you know the eye colors of the baby's parents and grandparents, you can make an educated guess about what their eye color might be.",
                        "answers": [
