                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nFirst, we need to understand what is meant by \"sensing visual things.\" This refers to the ability to see and perceive visual information. \n\nA) Nerves: While nerves play a crucial role in transmitting signals from the eyes to the brain, they are not directly involved in sensing visual things. \n\nB) Tibia: The tibia is a bone in the leg and has no role in sensing visual things. \n\nC) Nostril: The nostrils are used for smelling and have no role in sensing visual things. \n\nD) Cornea: The cornea is a transparent layer at the front of the eye that helps to focus light onto the retina. It plays a crucial role in sensing visual things and is an important part of the visual system. \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is D) cornea.",
