                        "cot": "\n\nStep 1: Identify the question and the options given.\n\nQuestion: What is used for sensing visual things?\n\nOptions: \nA) nerves \nB) tibia \nC) nostril \nD) cornea \n\nStep 2: Eliminate the options that are clearly not related to sensing visual things.\n\nOption B (tibia) and Option C (nostril) are not related to sensing visual things, so we can eliminate them.\n\nStep 3: Consider the remaining options and choose the one that is most closely related to sensing visual things.\n\nOption A (nerves) is involved in transmitting signals from the eyes to the brain, but it is not directly involved in sensing visual things. Option D (cornea) is the clear outer layer of the eye that helps to focus light onto the retina, which is responsible for sensing visual things. Therefore, the correct answer is D) cornea.",
