                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "A) Nerves - Nerves are responsible for transmitting signals from various parts of the body to the brain, including visual information. However, they are not the primary sensory organ for vision.\n\nB) Tibia - The tibia is a bone in the lower leg and is not related to vision.\n\nC) Nostril - The nostril is part of the nose and is responsible for the sense of smell, not vision.\n\nD) Cornea - The cornea is the transparent front part of the eye that covers the iris, pupil, and anterior chamber. It plays a significant role in focusing light onto the retina, which then sends visual information to the brain via the optic nerve.\n\nBased on this information, the correct answer is:\n\nD) Cornea",
