                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nFirst, we know that both humans and chickens have mothers, so option A is not the correct answer.\n\nSecond, fertilization in humans and chickens is different. In humans, fertilization occurs internally, where the sperm meets the egg inside the female reproductive system. In chickens, fertilization occurs externally, where the male deposits sperm onto the female's cloaca (a common opening for the reproductive, digestive, and urinary systems) and the sperm travels up to fertilize the egg as it is laid. Therefore, option B is the correct answer.\n\nOption C is not relevant to the question since it is not related to the process of birth.\n\nFinally, option D is also not relevant to the question since it refers to the hard shell of the egg, which is not related to the process of birth in either humans or chickens.",
