                        "cot": " In order for any animal to be born, there must first be fertilization. This is when the sperm from the father meets the egg from the mother. In chickens, the father's role is to simply provide the sperm. The mother then lays the egg and incubates it until it hatches. In humans, the father also provides the sperm, but the mother's role is much more hands on. The mother's body must go through many changes in order for the baby to develop properly and be born.",
