                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "How does birth in humans differ from birth in chickens?\nA) Who gives birth?\nB) How fertilization occurs?\nC) Who is the father?\nD) What is the role of the hard shell?\n\nStep-by-step reasoning:\n- A) Mother: In both humans and chickens, the mother gives birth.\n- B) Fertilization: In humans, fertilization occurs internally, while in chickens it occurs externally.\n- C) Father: In both humans and chickens, there is a father involved in fertilization.\n- D) the hard shell: The hard shell is a unique feature of chicken eggs, but it does not play a role in the actual birth process.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is B) Fertilization.",
                        "answers": [
