                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: Helium is a gas that is lighter than air and is commonly used to fill balloons. Heating a gas causes its particles to move faster and spread out, which can affect the volume of the gas.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What happens to the volume of a gas when it is heated?\n2. How does the volume of a balloon filled with helium change when it is heated?\n3. What is the effect of the fireplace on the balloons filled with helium?\n\nAnswering the sub-questions:\n1. When a gas is heated, its particles move faster and spread out, which increases the volume of the gas.\n2. The volume of a balloon filled with helium will increase when it is heated because the helium particles inside the balloon will move faster and spread out.\n3. The fireplace will heat the air in the living room, causing the air to expand and become less dense. The less dense air will rise, and the balloons filled with helium will also rise due to their buoyancy. As the balloons rise, they will encounter the hotter air near the ceiling, which will cause the helium inside the balloons to expand and increase the volume of the balloons. Therefore, the balloons will expand. \n\nAnswer: A) expand.",
