                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": " \n\nNuclear power plants require uranium, which is a radioactive element. In order for uranium to be useful as fuel, it must first be mined. Once it is mined, the uranium must be enriched, which is a process of increasing the concentration of uranium-235. \n\nUranium-235 is the isotope of uranium that is used in nuclear reactors. It is a fissile material, meaning that it can be split into smaller atoms in a nuclear fission reaction. \n\nIn a nuclear reactor, uranium-235 atoms are bombarded with neutrons. This causes the uranium-235 atoms to split, or fission. When the uranium-235 atoms split, they release energy in the form of heat and radiation. \n\nThe heat is used to generate steam. The steam turns turbines, which generate electricity. \n\nSo, in order for nuclear power to function, uranium must first be mined.",
