                        "cot": "Step 1: Identify the situation\n- There was a torrential downpour over a week.\n\nStep 2: Identify the location\n- The location is the man's backyard.\n\nStep 3: Identify the object being observed\n- The object being observed is the pond in the man's backyard.\n\nStep 4: Determine the state of the pond\n- The question asks for the state of the pond after the torrential downpour.\n- The options are: melted, dehydrated, bloated, and salted.\n\nStep 5: Eliminate options that do not make sense\n- Melted does not make sense because ponds do not melt.\n- Dehydrated does not make sense because ponds do not get dehydrated.\n- Salted does not make sense because there is no indication that salt was added to the pond.\n- Bloated makes sense because after a heavy rain, ponds can become bloated or swollen due to the excess water.\n\nStep 6: Choose the correct answer\n- The correct answer is C) bloated.",
