                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: People are born with certain innate characteristics, such as eye color and natural abilities, but other characteristics are developed over time through various factors such as environment and experiences.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What are genetics?\n- Genetics are the inherited traits passed down from biological parents to their offspring.\n\n2. What are skills?\n- Skills are abilities that are learned and developed through practice and experience.\n\n3. What are physical attributes?\n- Physical attributes are characteristics of a person's body, such as hair color, eye color, and body shape.\n\n4. Can genetics influence the development of skills?\n- Yes, genetics can play a role in the development of certain skills, such as musical ability or athletic prowess.\n\n5. Can physical attributes be changed through external factors?\n- Some physical attributes can be changed through external factors, such as hair color through dyeing or body shape through exercise and diet.\n\nAnswer: People are not born with skills and physical attributes that can be developed or changed over time through various factors such as environment and experiences. Therefore, options B and C are characteristics that people are not born with.",
