                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "The correct answer is B) the moon is brighter than stars.\n\nTo understand why, we need to consider the distance between the observer and the light source. The sun is always bright because it is the closest star to Earth and emits a large amount of light. The moon, while not a source of light itself, reflects sunlight and appears bright in the night sky. However, stars are much further away than the moon and therefore appear dimmer in comparison. A floodlight, while not as far away as stars, is still not as close as the moon and therefore may also appear less bright. Therefore, the correct answer is B) the moon is brighter than stars.",
                        "answers": [
