                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "C) reverberations to strike the eardrum.\n\nWhen a drum is banged, it creates sound waves that travel through the air. These sound waves cause the drumhead to vibrate, which in turn creates vibrations in the air. These vibrations are known as reverberations. When the reverberations reach our ears, they cause our eardrums to vibrate, which our brain interprets as sound. Therefore, banging on a drum causes reverberations to strike the eardrum. Options A, B, and D are not directly related to the act of banging on a drum.",
