                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "What is the effect of banging on a drum?\n\nTo answer this question, we need to consider the options given and determine which one is the most accurate.\n\nA) Music to be loud - This option is partially correct. Banging on a drum can make music louder, but it is not the only effect.\n\nB) Music to be appealing - This option is not accurate. Banging on a drum does not necessarily make music more appealing.\n\nC) Reverberations to strike the eardrum - This option is the most accurate. Banging on a drum creates sound waves that travel through the air and cause the drumhead to vibrate. These vibrations create sound waves that travel to the ear and strike the eardrum, allowing us to hear the sound.\n\nD) Concerts to sell out - This option is not accurate. Banging on a drum may be a part of a concert, but it does not directly cause concerts to sell out.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is C) Reverberations to strike the eardrum.",
