                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Rephrased question: What causes the seasons by rotating on its axis?\n\nStep-by-step reasoning:\n- Seasons are the changes in weather and temperature that occur throughout the year.\n- These changes are caused by the amount of sunlight and heat that different parts of the Earth receive.\n- The amount of sunlight and heat depends on the angle at which the Sun's rays hit the Earth's surface.\n- This angle changes throughout the year because the Earth rotates on its axis and revolves around the Sun.\n- Therefore, the answer is D) The Sun, as it is the source of the sunlight and heat that causes the seasons.\n\nAnswer: D) The Sun.",
