                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": " Where is water typically found? In its liquid form, water is typically found in lakes, rivers, and the ocean. In its solid form, water is found in ice and snow. So where might water be found in its gas form?\n\nOne place water can be found in its gas form is inside a disc golf driver. When the disc golf driver is hit, the water inside turns to gas and is released. Another place water can be found in its gas form is inside of a brass pipe. When the brass pipe is heated, the water inside turns to gas and is released. Finally, water can be found in its gas form a mile up in the sky. This is because water vapor is one of the gases that makes up the Earth's atmosphere.",
                        "answers": [
