                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Water in its gas form is known as water vapor. It is a colorless and odorless gas that is formed when liquid water evaporates. Therefore, the location of water in its gas form depends on the conditions of temperature and pressure.\n\nOption A, inside a disc golf driver, is not a possible location for water in its gas form as it is a solid object and cannot contain water vapor.\n\nOption B, inside of a brass pipe, is also not a possible location for water in its gas form unless the temperature and pressure inside the pipe are such that the liquid water has evaporated and turned into water vapor.\n\nOption C, a mile up in the sky, is a possible location for water in its gas form. At high altitudes, the temperature and pressure are such that liquid water can evaporate and turn into water vapor. This is why clouds are formed at high altitudes.\n\nOption D, inside a leather baseball, is not a possible location for water in its gas form as the leather baseball is a solid object and cannot contain water vapor.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is C) a mile up in the sky.",
