                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: Water can exist in three states: solid (ice), liquid (water), and gas (water vapor).\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What is water vapor?\n2. What are the conditions required for water to exist in its gas form?\n3. Can water vapor be found in different locations?\n\nAnswers:\n1. Water vapor is the gaseous form of water.\n2. Water can exist in its gas form when it reaches its boiling point (100\u00b0C or 212\u00b0F) and turns into steam. This can happen when water is heated or when it is exposed to high temperatures and low pressures.\n3. Yes, water vapor can be found in different locations depending on the conditions. For example:\n- Water vapor can be found in the atmosphere, where it makes up a small percentage of the air we breathe.\n- Water vapor can be found in clouds, which are made up of tiny water droplets or ice crystals.\n- Water vapor can be found in steam, which is used to power turbines and generate electricity.\n- Water vapor can be found in humid environments, such as rainforests or saunas.\n\nAnswer to the original question:\nWater can be located in its gas form a mile up in the sky (option C).",
