                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: Can you explain the question again, please?\n\nProfessor: Sure. The question is asking where water can be found in its gas form.\n\nStudent: Okay, got it. So, the options are inside a disc golf driver, inside of a brass pipe, a mile up in the sky, and inside a leather baseball. Which one is the correct answer?\n\nProfessor: The correct answer is C) a mile up in the sky.\n\nStudent: Why is that the correct answer?\n\nProfessor: Water in its gas form is called water vapor. It is a gas that is formed when water evaporates. When the sun heats up the water on the earth's surface, it turns into water vapor and rises up into the atmosphere. As it rises, it cools down and condenses into clouds. So, a mile up in the sky is where you would find water in its gas form.\n\nStudent: Oh, I see. So, the other options are incorrect because they don't have anything to do with water vapor?\n\nProfessor: Yes, that's correct. Water vapor is not found inside a disc golf driver, inside of a brass pipe, or inside a leather baseball. Those options are just there to confuse you.",
