                        "cot": "\n\nFirst, we know that pesticides are used on crops to grow food safely. \n\nNext, we are told that flooding can cause something to become poisonous. \n\nOut of the options given, the only one that makes sense in this context is C) Runoff. \n\nWhen it floods, the water can wash away the pesticides from the crops and carry them into nearby bodies of water, creating pesticide runoff. This runoff can then contaminate the water and make it poisonous for aquatic life and potentially harmful for humans who consume it.",
