                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: Pesticides are chemicals used to kill pests and protect crops from damage. When it rains, the pesticides can be washed off the crops and into nearby bodies of water, causing pollution and potential harm to aquatic life.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What happens to pesticides when it rains?\n2. Where do the pesticides go when they are washed off the crops?\n3. What are the potential effects of pesticides in bodies of water?\n\nAnswers:\n1. When it rains, pesticides can be washed off the crops and into nearby bodies of water.\n2. The pesticides can go into nearby bodies of water through runoff.\n3. Pesticides in bodies of water can cause pollution and harm to aquatic life, as well as potentially contaminate drinking water sources.\n\nAnswer to original question: C) Runoff",
