                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "it is important to note that the formation of fossil fuels, such as coal, oil, and natural gas, takes millions of years. The earliest humans, Homo habilis, evolved around 2.8 million years ago, while the formation of fossil fuels began around 360 million years ago. Therefore, humans predate fossil fuel formation.\n\nHowever, it is possible that there were some small amounts of fossil fuels in the ground when humans evolved, as the formation process is ongoing and continuous. But significant supplies of fossil fuels accumulated over time, and were not present in large quantities when humans first evolved. Therefore, the correct answer is C) significant supplies accumulated prior.",
