                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Fossil fuels, such as coal, oil, and natural gas, are formed from the remains of ancient plants and animals that lived millions of years ago. The process of fossil fuel formation takes millions of years and involves heat, pressure, and chemical reactions.\n\nHumans, on the other hand, evolved much more recently. The first anatomically modern humans (Homo sapiens) appeared around 300,000 years ago.\n\nGiven this information, we can conclude that significant supplies of fossil fuels had already accumulated in the ground before humans evolved. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\nC) significant supplies accumulated prior",
