                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Plan:\n1. Research the timeline of human evolution and the formation of fossil fuels.\n2. Determine if there was enough time for significant supplies of fossil fuels to accumulate prior to human evolution.\n3. Consider any evidence or theories that suggest humans may have used or interacted with fossil fuels before modern times.\n\nAnswer: \nB) Humans predate fossil fuel formation. Fossil fuels, such as coal, oil, and natural gas, are formed from the remains of ancient plants and animals that lived millions of years ago. The earliest humans, Homo habilis, evolved around 2.8 million years ago, while the formation of fossil fuels began around 360 million years ago. Therefore, humans predate the formation of fossil fuels.",
