                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Additional knowledge: Fossil fuels are formed from the remains of dead plants and animals that have been buried and subjected to heat and pressure over millions of years. The three main types of fossil fuels are coal, oil, and natural gas.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. When did humans evolve?\n2. When were fossil fuels formed?\n3. Is there evidence of fossil fuels existing before humans discovered and used them?\n\nAnswers:\n1. Humans evolved around 200,000 years ago.\n2. Fossil fuels were formed over millions of years, with coal being formed around 300 million years ago, oil around 100 million years ago, and natural gas around 50 million years ago.\n3. Yes, there is evidence of fossil fuels existing before humans discovered and used them. For example, coal deposits have been found in rocks that are over 300 million years old, and oil and natural gas have been found in rock formations that are tens of millions of years old.",
