                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "The correct answer is C) genetic contributors had long ears.\n\nExplanation:\n\nLong ears in rabbits are a physical trait that is determined by genetics. DNA contains the instructions for the development of physical traits, including the length of the ears. Therefore, if a rabbit has long ears, it is because it inherited the genetic information for long ears from its parents. Option A is incorrect because all rabbits are born with ears, but the length of the ears is determined by genetics. Option B is also incorrect because the amount of food a rabbit eats does not affect the length of its ears. Option D is not a sufficient condition for a rabbit to have long ears because both parents could have short ears, but the rabbit could still inherit the genetic information for long ears from a grandparent or other ancestor.",
