                    {
                        "id": "a36fe715-58b0-4f5c-9b98-3ba1f8b56e02",
                        "fragments_version": "0.01",
                        "instruction": "qa-16",
                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Question: What determines whether a rabbit will have long ears?\n\nHelpful knowledge: DNA is responsible for passing on genetic traits from parents to offspring. Rabbits are a species of mammal that are known for their long ears.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What is DNA?\n2. How are genetic traits passed down from parents to offspring?\n3. Are long ears a common trait among rabbits?\n4. Can a rabbit with short-eared parents still have long ears?\n\nAnswers:\n1. DNA stands for deoxyribonucleic acid and is a molecule that contains genetic instructions for the development and function of all living organisms.\n2. Genetic traits are passed down from parents to offspring through the transmission of DNA. Each parent contributes half of their DNA to their offspring, which determines their physical and behavioral characteristics.\n3. Yes, long ears are a common trait among rabbits. In fact, rabbits are known for their long ears, which help them to detect predators and regulate their body temperature.\n4. Yes, a rabbit with short-eared parents can still have long ears if they inherit the necessary genetic contributors from their grandparents or other ancestors. Genetic traits can be passed down through multiple generations, so it is possible for a trait to skip a generation and reappear in a later one.",
                        "answers": [
                            {
                                "id": "29895606-66bf-4124-afc9-209141de1994",
                                "answer_extraction": "kojima-A-D",
                                "answer_extraction_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}{cot}\n{answer_extraction}",
                                "answer_extraction_text": "",
                                "answer": "C) genetic contributors had long ears. The presence of specific genes for long ears in a rabbit's DNA is what determines whether or not they will have long ears.",
                                "correct_answer": true
                            }
                        ],
