                        "cot_trigger": "kojima-01",
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": " \n\nFirst, we need to understand what phloem is. Phloem is the part of a plant that helps to transport food and water throughout the plant. \n\nNext, we need to think about how phloem moves things around a plant. Phloem uses a process called translocation to move food and water throughout the plant. Translocation is the movement of molecules from one place to another. \n\nNow, let's think about how this compares to blood in a body. Blood moves throughout the body to transport oxygen and nutrients to the cells. Blood uses a process called circulation to move oxygen and nutrients to the cells. Circulation is the movement of blood through the body. \n\nWe can see that phloem and blood both use a process of movement to transport molecules from one place to another. However, blood uses circulation to move oxygen and nutrients to the cells, while phloem uses translocation to move food and water throughout the plant.",
