                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "The correct answer is D) toes are wiggled.\n\nMuscles are responsible for producing movement in the body. When a muscle contracts, it pulls on the bone it is attached to, causing movement. In the case of wiggling toes, the muscles in the foot and lower leg contract, causing the bones in the toes to move.\n\nOption A) Arms are resting - This is not an example of movement produced by muscles. When the arms are resting, there is no muscle contraction causing movement.\n\nOption B) Hair is growing - This is not an example of movement produced by muscles. Hair growth is a natural process that occurs without muscle involvement.\n\nOption C) Smiles are invisible - This is not an example of movement produced by muscles. While smiling does involve muscle contraction in the face, it is not a visible movement of bones in the body.",
