                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Plan:\n1. Understand the life cycle of a flower.\n2. Identify the purpose of each stage in the life cycle.\n3. Determine which purpose aligns with the options given in the question.\n4. Choose the option that best fits the purpose of the flower's life cycle.\n\nAnswer: B) be successfully fertilized.\n\nExplanation:\n1. The life cycle of a flower begins with a seed, which germinates and grows into a plant.\n2. The plant produces flowers, which contain reproductive organs.\n3. Pollination occurs when pollen from the male reproductive organ (stamen) is transferred to the female reproductive organ (pistil) of the same or a different flower.\n4. Fertilization occurs when the sperm from the pollen combines with the egg in the ovary of the flower, resulting in the formation of a seed.\n5. The purpose of the flower's life cycle is to reproduce and ensure the survival of the species.\n6. Option B, \"be successfully fertilized,\" aligns with the purpose of the flower's life cycle, as it is necessary for the production of seeds and the continuation of the species. Therefore, the correct answer is B) be successfully fertilized.",
