                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: Flowers are reproductive structures of plants that produce seeds for the next generation. \n\nSub-questions:\n1. What is the purpose of a flower?\n2. How do flowers reproduce?\n3. What happens after a flower is fertilized?\n\nAnswers:\n1. The purpose of a flower is to reproduce and produce seeds for the next generation of plants.\n2. Flowers reproduce through pollination, where pollen from the male reproductive organ (stamen) is transferred to the female reproductive organ (pistil) either by wind, water, or animals.\n3. After a flower is fertilized, the ovary at the base of the pistil develops into a fruit that contains seeds. The flower then withers and dies, having completed its life work of reproducing. \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is B) be successfully fertilized.",
