                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: Earthworms are known for their ability to burrow through soil and create tunnels. They are important for soil health and nutrient cycling.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What is the habitat of earthworms?\n2. What is the purpose of earthworm tunnels?\n3. What is the composition of ice, dirt, water, and concrete?\n\nAnswers:\n1. Earthworms live in soil, leaf litter, and other organic matter.\n2. Earthworm tunnels help to aerate the soil, improve water infiltration, and mix organic matter into the soil.\n3. Ice is made of frozen water molecules, dirt is a mixture of sand, silt, and clay particles, water is a liquid composed of hydrogen and oxygen molecules, and concrete is a mixture of cement, sand, and gravel.\n\nConclusion:\nBased on the sub-questions and answers, we can conclude that earthworms create tunnels in dirt, but not in ice, water, or concrete.",
