                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "\n\nFirst, we need to understand what happens when an organism dies. Its body starts to decompose, which means that its tissues break down into simpler compounds. This process is carried out by decomposers, such as bacteria, fungi, and worms.\n\nAmong these decomposers, worms play an important role in returning nutrients from dead organisms to the soil. They do this by eating the decomposing matter and breaking it down further in their digestive system. As a result, the nutrients that were locked up in the dead organism's tissues become available to other living organisms in the soil.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is B) decomposition.",
                        "answers": [
