                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: Professor, can you explain the question again?\n\nProfessor: Sure, the question is asking what it's called when worms eat dead organisms and return the nutrients to the soil.\n\nStudent: Okay, so what does regurgitation mean?\n\nProfessor: Regurgitation is when an animal brings up food from its stomach to chew it again. It's not related to this question.\n\nStudent: And what about burial?\n\nProfessor: Burial is when something is covered with soil or other material. It's not related to this question either.\n\nStudent: So, it's either decomposition or recycling?\n\nProfessor: Yes, that's correct. Decomposition is the process of breaking down dead organisms into simpler substances. Recycling is the process of reusing materials to make something new. Which one do you think it is?\n\nStudent: I think it's recycling.\n\nProfessor: Actually, it's decomposition. When worms eat dead organisms, they break them down into simpler substances that can be used by plants to grow. This is an important part of the nutrient cycle in ecosystems.",
