                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: Can you explain what you mean by \"food production\" in a leaf?\n\nProfessor: Sure, in a process called photosynthesis, plants use energy from sunlight to convert carbon dioxide and water into glucose, which is a type of sugar that the plant uses as food.\n\nStudent: Okay, so what happens in a leaf during photosynthesis?\n\nProfessor: During photosynthesis, the chloroplasts in the leaf cells absorb light energy and use it to convert carbon dioxide and water into glucose. This process also releases oxygen as a byproduct.\n\nStudent: So, which option is the correct answer?\n\nProfessor: The correct answer is A) nutrient making process, which refers to the process of photosynthesis in which glucose is produced as a nutrient for the plant. Option B) the breathing, refers to the process of respiration in which the plant takes in oxygen and releases carbon dioxide. Option C) the respiration, refers to the process of breaking down glucose to release energy for the plant. Option D) the digestion, is not a process that occurs in a leaf.",
