                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Helpful knowledge: Inheritance refers to the passing down of traits from parents to offspring through genes.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. Which of the given characteristics are determined by genes?\n2. Can the length of hair, number of friends, number of nails, or length of shirt be influenced by environmental factors?\n3. Are any of these characteristics sex-linked traits?\n\nAnswers:\n1. All of the given characteristics are determined by genes to some extent. Hair length and nail number are determined by multiple genes, while the number of friends and length of shirt are not directly determined by genes but may be influenced by genetic factors such as personality traits or body size.\n2. Hair length and nail number can be influenced by environmental factors such as nutrition and grooming habits. The number of friends and length of shirt are more directly influenced by environmental factors such as social opportunities and clothing choices.\n3. None of the given characteristics are sex-linked traits, meaning they are not determined by genes on the sex chromosomes.",
