                        "cot_trigger": null,
                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "The question is: What is the effect of evaporation?\n\nHelpful knowledge: Evaporation is the process by which a liquid turns into a gas or vapor. It occurs when the molecules in a liquid gain enough energy to break free and become a gas.\n\nSub-questions:\n1. What happens to the water molecules during evaporation?\n2. What are some examples of where evaporation occurs?\n3. How does evaporation affect the environment?\n\nAnswers:\n1. During evaporation, the water molecules gain enough energy to break free from the liquid and become a gas or vapor.\n2. Examples of where evaporation occurs include bodies of water such as lakes, rivers, and oceans, as well as wet surfaces like roads, sidewalks, and roofs.\n3. Evaporation can have various effects on the environment. It can cause puddles to become dried out mud (A), which can be beneficial for plants that thrive in drier conditions. However, it can also lead to droughts and water shortages in areas where water is scarce. Evaporation does not directly cause fields of crops to grow faster (B) or flowers to bloom abundantly (C), but it can contribute to the overall health of plants by providing them with water through the water cycle. Evaporation also does not fill up irrigation ponds (D), as these ponds are typically filled with water from other sources such as rivers or wells.",
