                        "cot_trigger_template": "{instruction}\n\n{question}\n{answer_choices}\n\n{cot_trigger}",
                        "prompt_text": "",
                        "cot": "Student: Professor, can you explain what evaporation is?\n\nProfessor: Sure, evaporation is the process by which a liquid turns into a gas or vapor.\n\nStudent: So, does evaporation cause puddles to become dried out mud?\n\nProfessor: Yes, that's correct. When water in a puddle is exposed to heat, it evaporates and turns into water vapor, leaving behind the solid particles that were dissolved in the water. This is why the remaining water in the puddle becomes more concentrated and eventually dries out, leaving behind mud.\n\nStudent: Does evaporation have any effect on fields of crops?\n\nProfessor: Yes, it does. When water evaporates from the soil, it leaves behind the nutrients that are essential for plant growth. This helps the crops to grow faster and healthier.\n\nStudent: What about flowers? Does evaporation have any effect on them?\n\nProfessor: Yes, it does. When water evaporates from the soil, it creates a humid environment that is ideal for flowers to bloom. This is why you often see flowers blooming abundantly after a rain shower.\n\nStudent: And finally, does evaporation fill up irrigation ponds?\n\nProfessor: No, evaporation does not fill up irrigation ponds. In fact, it has the opposite effect. When water in an irrigation pond evaporates, it reduces the amount of water available for irrigation. This is why farmers need to constantly monitor the water levels in their ponds and replenish them as needed.",
