                        "cot": "Rephrased question: Which family member's chance of inheriting a trait can be calculated using a Punnett square?\n\nStep-by-step reasoning:\n- A Punnett square is a tool used to predict the probability of offspring inheriting certain traits from their parents.\n- Therefore, the family member whose chance of inheriting a trait can be calculated using a Punnett square must be someone who is a potential parent of the offspring.\n- Out of the options given, only the father and mother are potential parents.\n- Therefore, the answer is either A) mother or D) father.\n\nAnswer: D) father.",
